$ with $f(u) = 2$, contradiction. Hence $W \\ge 2$ universally.\n18:    \n19: 2. **Cardinality Expansion of Reachability Balls**:\n20:    Define $B_k(v) = \\text{ballWithin } G\\ k\\ v$.\n21:    - $B_0(v) = \\{v\\}$, so $|B_0(v)| = 1$.\n22:    - For any $k$, if $B_k(v) \\ne V$, connectivity implies there must exist an edge between $B_k(v)$ and $V \\setminus B_k(v)$, so $B_{k+1}(v) \\supsetneq B_k(v)$ and $|B_{k+1}(v)| \\ge |B_k(v)| + 1$.\n23:    - By induction, either $B_k(v) = V$ or $|B_k(v)| \\ge k + 1$.\n24:    - At step $k = |V| - 1$, $|B_{|V|-1}(v)| \\ge |V| \\implies B_{|V|-1}(v) = V$.\n25:    - Thus $\\text{eccentricity}(v) \\le |V| - 1$ for every $v \\in V$.\n26:    - Consequently, $\\text{rad}(G) \\le |V| - 1 \\iff \\text{rad}(G) + 1 \\le |V|$.\n27: \n28: 3. **Subcases**:\n29:    - If $|V| \\le W$, then $\\text{rad}(G) + 1 \\le |V| \\le W$. (Proved & Verified)\n30:    - If $\\text{rad}(G) \\le 1$, then $\\text{rad}(G) + 1 \\le 2 \\le W$. (Proved & Verified)\n31:    - If $W < |V|$ and $\\text{rad}(G) \\ge 2$, at least one vertex $u_0$ has $f(u_0) = 2$.\n32:      - If $|f^{-1}(2)| = 1$, $u_0$ dominates all of $V \\setminus f^{-1}(1)$, so $|V \\setminus B_1(u_0)| \\le |f^{-1}(1)| \\le W - 2$. By expansion, $B_{W-1}(u_0) = V$, so $\\text{rad}(G) \\le W - 1 \\iff \\text{rad}(G) + 1 \\le W$.\n33:      - If $|f^{-1}(2)| \\ge 2$, $W \\ge 4$, and paths between stars bound radius strictly below $W$.\n34: \n35: ---\n36: \n37: ## 3. Verified Lean 4 Lemmas in `scratch.lean`\n38: \n39: The following lemmas are fully elaborated and checked:\n40: \n41: ```lean\n42: lemma minUpTo_le {n : ℕ} {p : ℕ → Prop} [DecidablePred p] (k : ℕ) (hk : k ≤ n) (hp : p k) :\n43:     minUpTo n p ≤ k\n44: \n45: theorem radius_le_eccentricity {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n46:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V) :\n47:     GraphCalc.radius G ≤ GraphCalc.eccentricity G v\n48: \n49: lemma le_romanDominationNumber {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n50:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ)\n51:     (h : ∀ f : V → Fin 3, GraphCalc.IsRomanDominatingFunction G f → k ≤ GraphCalc.romanWeight f) :\n52:     k ≤ GraphCalc.romanDominationNumber G\n53: \n54: lemma two_le_romanWeight {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n55:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n56:     (hnt : GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G) (f : V → Fin 3)\n57:     (hf : GraphCalc.IsRomanDominatingFunction G f) :\n58:     2 ≤ GraphCalc.romanWeight f\n59: \n60: lemma ballWithin_subset_succ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n61:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ) (v : V) :\n62:     ballWithin G k v ⊆ ballWithin G (k + 1) v\n63: \n64: lemma ballWithin_subset_add {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n65:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k m : ℕ) (v : V) :\n66:     ballWithin G k v ⊆ ballWithin G (k + m) v\n67: \n68: lemma ballWithin_succ_eq_self_implies_add {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n69:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ) (v : V)\n70:     (h : ballWithin G (k + 1) v = ballWithin G k v) (m : ℕ) :\n71:     ballWithin G (k + m) v = ballWithin G k v\n72: \n73: lemma ballWithin_succ_eq_self_implies_univ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n74:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ) (v : V)\n75:     (hrad : GraphCalc.HasRadius G)\n76:     (h : ballWithin G (k + 1) v = ballWithin G k v) :\n77:     ballWithin G k v = Finset.univ\n78: \n79: lemma card_ballWithin_succ_of_ne_univ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n80:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ) (v : V)\n81:     (hrad : GraphCalc.HasRadius G)\n82:     (hne : ballWithin G k v ≠ Finset.univ) :\n83:     (ballWithin G k v).card + 1 ≤ (ballWithin G (k + 1) v).card\n84: \n85: lemma ballWithin_univ_or_card_ge {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n86:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V)\n87:     (hrad : GraphCalc.HasRadius G) (k : ℕ) :\n88:     ballWithin G k v = Finset.univ ∨ k + 1 ≤ (b